```
Add an arrow glyph? Use ::after? The transition text is the payload; prefix "→ " via CSS ::before? Simply include in content? I set text to payload; add `::before { content: "→ "; }`? Actually visually: [step1] —payload→ [step2]. Add ::after "→"? Put payload + arrow. Let me: `.trace-transition::after { content: " →"; color: var(--map-text-muted); }` Hmm arrow should be at end pointing to next. Fine.

Region header scale + summary:
```css
.canvas-region > header { ... existing; transform: scale(var(--label-scale)); transform-origin: left top; }
```
Careful: transform scale on header with position absolute; scaling enlarges beyond header box — fine visually.

Region summary styles:
```css
.region-summary { color: var(--map-text-muted); left: 14px; position: absolute; right: 14px; top: 34px; transform: scale(var(--label-scale)); transform-origin: left top; }
.region-summary p { font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
.region-composition { color: #8fa0a4; }
.region-attention { color: var(--map-attention); }
.region-key-objects { color: var(--map-text-soft); }
.region-crossing { color: #78898e; }
.canvas-region.emphasis-muted .region-summary { opacity: .55; }
```
Hmm, at landscape the summary should be more prominent — bigger? The label-scale handles size. At landscape header hides span/small already (`.canvas-region.zoom-landscape > header span, small {display:none}`). Composition + key objects show. Good.

But wait: summary shows at ALL zoom levels now — at component/operational, objects inside region are fully rendered; region summary at top would overlap objects? Region header occupies top padding (46-54px). Summary top: 34px adds ~3 lines → needs ~34+50 = 84px but padding only 54. Overlap risk with objects at depth-0 region header area. Options: show summary line only at architecture/landscape (where it matters: default density + hidden objects). At component/operational: hide summary. CSS:
```css
.canvas-region .region-summary { display: none; }
.canvas-region.zoom-landscape .region-summary, .canvas-region.zoom-architecture .region-summary { display: block; }
```
At architecture, region padding-top is 54 (depth 0) — summary needs ~2 lines (composition + attention) ≈ 40px starting at 34 → ends 74 > 54. Hmm overlap with first object. Mitigate: summary only 1 line at architecture (composition + attention combined?) — region-node renders composition + attention (2 lines at most, attention rare). Increase region padding top for depth 0: 54 → 88? That changes layout geometry (ELK padding) — fine, adjust regionOptions padding top depth0 → 96, depth>0 → 60. Then header (top 11) + summary (top 36, up to 2 lines ≈ 42px) ends ~78 < 96. ✓

Landscape: 3-4 lines (composition, attention, key objects, crossing) ≈ 88px — landscape hides most objects but important ones still inside; padding 96 covers ~4 lines. OK good — set padding top: depth 0: 100, nested: 64.

Update regionOptions padding accordingly:
`"elk.padding": `[top=${depth === 0 ? 100 : 64},left=26,bottom=26,right=26]``.

Wait, but nested regions (depth 1+) inside a region also have their own header + summary — they nest inside parent region's content area; their headers consume their own padding. OK.

Now also the canvas-region header at landscape currently hides span/small — keep name only. Good.

