Wait — should this pan happen in ALL modes when clicking canvas nodes? Clicking a visible node is already on-screen; panning would be annoying. Only pan when the object is NOT from a canvas click... can't distinguish easily. Restrict: pan only in trace mode (corridor navigation):

In select: `if (selection?.kind === "object") { setTimeout(() => centerOnObject(selection.id), 80) }` only when current interaction mode is trace. Need layout + instance + surface. centerOnObject: 
```ts
function centerOnObject(objectId: string) {
  const instance = instanceRef.current; const surface = surfaceRef.current; const rect = layout?.objectRects[objectId];
